    "description": {
      "chat": "",
      "unidentified": "",
      "value": "<p>Choose one creature from the 7th-level list, 1d3 creatures of the same kind from the 6th-level list, or 1d4+1 creatures of the same kind using any combination of lower-level lists. One suitable corpse is required per creature.</p><p>The 7th-level list allows: banshee, shade, or ghost from a humanoid of CR 5 for banshee, CR 5 for shade, or an eligible Charisma 6+ creature of CR 4 for ghost; crypt fiend from a nerubian of CR 7 or 8; forsaken from a humanoid of CR 7 or 8; ghoul or wraith from a humanoid or monstrous humanoid of CR 7; skeletal mage from a humanoid of CR 6 or 7; skeletal warrior from a humanoid or monstrous humanoid of CR 7 or 8; or withered from an aberration, animal, dragon, fey, magical beast, plant, or other monstrous creature of CR 7. Eligible ghost base types are aberration, animal, giant, humanoid, magical beast, monstrous humanoid, or plant; a summoned ghost has malevolence, horrific appearance, and corrupting gaze.</p><p>Summons act immediately on your turn and obey communicated directions. They do not count against your control limit, cannot fuel <em>death pact</em>, summon or conjure, teleport, or travel between planes, and require a supporting environment. At the end, they collapse or vanish and leave remains unusable for further undead magic; every source corpse is despoiled.</p><p><strong>Automation boundary:</strong> Roll the quantity, choose valid lower tiers, validate and consume every corpse, create and control each temporary undead, and remove all summons and unusable remains manually.</p>"
    },
